  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "coI6I68TW1H5eNypLVa0g/J0XhA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:51.050Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "ELCA Group is recorded as the largest independent Swiss IT firm, 2,200-plus experts across Pully/Lausanne and four further cities, dual-certified with Camunda Silver alongside its Flowable listing. The record's own summary of the consequence is short: enterprise scale.\n\nIndependence is worth separating from size, because the two criteria pull in different directions here. Independence is a positive the screen values elsewhere \u2014 it is exactly what Truewind lost when VINCI acquired it, and what makes foreign ownership a disqualifier for NTT Data Spain. An independent firm decides its own technology positioning without a parent's alliance framework. But at this headcount the decision still routes through architecture review and alliance management rather than a delivery lead, which is what puts the row at priority 3.\n\nThe dual Camunda and Flowable position means the technical seam is the same one the corpus describes repeatedly: orchestration engines that hold process state as mutable, purgeable rows, with no append-only record of what was decided. ELCA has that gap in two platforms and the Swiss financial-sector client base where the question is already funded \u2014 which is why this is a deferral on entry cost, not a rejection on fit. Provenance: Flowable Partner Finder, mined 2026-08-18, not imprint-swept.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- ELCA Group (CH Pully/Lausanne + 4 cities) \u2014 elca.ch\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> 2,200+ experts, largest independent Swiss IT firm. DUAL: Camunda Silver. Enterprise scale \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:51.050411Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:51.050415Z"
    }
  },
